(LST2-42 — `<action> each <variable> from <collection>` runs the action
 once per item, over a list literal, a range, and a list variable.
 The manual's own "Loop Expansion with Collections" examples.
 Also covers: LST2-43 (a list literal source), LST2-44 (a range source,
 inclusive at both ends), LST2-45 (a function call per item), LST2-46
 (`append each X from Y to Z`), LST2-47 (the `<action> each <var> from
 <collection>` syntax), LST2-48 (any list variable is a legal source),
 LST2-51 (print each), LST2-52 (function of each), LST2-53 (append each),
 LST2-55 (`print <func> of each ...` prints the returned values),
 LST2-56 (an empty collection does nothing).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox LST2-42.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
